    - Id: text_03
      Title: Items/InstrumentPanel
      Lines:
      - Speaker: 2
        DisplayName: PREVIEW
        Text: 'Discarded Electromechanical Instrument Panel


          Description:

          A bank of brass-rimmed analog gauges beneath a curved, dust-protective glass cover coated with space dust. Slender needles sit frozen against faded scales, with levers and tiny adjustment knobs protruding from the side. Aboard the colony ships of the old era, it served as the senses of an entire compartment, providing readings of pressure, energy flux, and temperature.


          Dismantling yields:

          Rolled Electromechanical Alloy Sheets x3

          Tinned Copper Wire & Windings x2

          Precision Drive Gear Blanks x1

          Heat-Resistant Ceramic Insulators x1

          Vulcanized Airtight Rubber Liners x1'
        UseCustomColor: 0
        CustomColor:
          R: 0.65
          G: 1
          B: 0.76
          A: 1
        WaitForContinue: 0
        DelayAfter: 0.15
      Choices:
      - Id: text_03_option_0
        Label: BACK TO ARCHIVE
        PlayerText: BACK TO ARCHIVE
        DisplayName: 
        UseCustomColor: 0
        CustomColor:
          R: 0.65
          G: 1
          B: 0.76
          A: 1
        NextNodeId: preview_home
        Conditions: []
        SetFlags: []
        Events: []
      NextNodeId: 
    - Id: text_04
      Title: Items/RadioReceiver
      Lines:
      - Speaker: 2
        DisplayName: PREVIEW
        Text: 'Vacuum-Tube Radio Receiver


          Description:

          A heavy cast-iron case houses several clear glass vacuum tubes behind its front grille. The tuning dial''s etched markings are worn, and much of the speaker diaphragm is dry and cracked. It was once the sole communications link for a distant interstellar colony, receiving broadcasts from the homeworld across the void. After the old era ended, this receiver became a symbol of romance. Now, it is only good for salvaging the copper and insulating components inside.


          Dismantling yields:

          Rolled Electromechanical Alloy Sheets x2

          Tinned Copper Wire & Windings x4

          Precision Drive Gear Blanks x1

          Heat-Resistant Ceramic Insulators x2

          Vulcanized Airtight Rubber Liners x1'
        UseCustomColor: 0
        CustomColor:
          R: 0.65
          G: 1
          B: 0.76
          A: 1
        WaitForContinue: 0
        DelayAfter: 0.15
      Choices:
      - Id: text_04_option_0
        Label: BACK TO ARCHIVE
        PlayerText: BACK TO ARCHIVE
        DisplayName: 
        UseCustomColor: 0
        CustomColor:
          R: 0.65
          G: 1
          B: 0.76
          A: 1
        NextNodeId: preview_home
        Conditions: []
        SetFlags: []
        Events: []
      NextNodeId: 
    - Id: text_05
      Title: Items/RelaySwitchingUnit
      Lines:
      - Speaker: 2
        DisplayName: PREVIEW
        Text: 'Electromechanical Relay Switching Unit


          Description:

          A boxy metal housing covered in scorch marks, densely packed with electromagnetic relays, copper terminals, and stepping dials. This was an ancient civilization''s primitive logic center, opening and closing contacts to transmit signals and coordinate the compartment''s electromechanical equipment. It could perform complex timing control without silicon chips. Remarkable.


          Dismantling yields:

          Rolled Electromechanical Alloy Sheets x2

          Tinned Copper Wire & Windings x2

          Precision Drive Gear Blanks x4

          Heat-Resistant Ceramic Insulators x1

          Vulcanized Airtight Rubber Liners x1'
        UseCustomColor: 0
        CustomColor:
          R: 0.65
          G: 1
          B: 0.76
          A: 1
        WaitForContinue: 0
        DelayAfter: 0.15
      Choices:
      - Id: text_05_option_0
        Label: BACK TO ARCHIVE
        PlayerText: BACK TO ARCHIVE
        DisplayName: 
        UseCustomColor: 0
        CustomColor:
          R: 0.65
          G: 1
          B: 0.76
          A: 1
        NextNodeId: preview_home
        Conditions: []
        SetFlags: []
        Events: []
      NextNodeId: 
    - Id: text_06
      Title: Items/FluidManifold
      Lines:
      - Speaker: 2
        DisplayName: PREVIEW
        Text: 'Old Compartment Fluid Manifold Assembly


          Description:

          A tangled cluster of metal pipes fitted with needle valves and corrugated pressure bellows. Hardened sealing gaskets still cling to its connections. It once carried oxygen, cooling water, and propellant, sustaining life within the compartment and keeping the engines running.


          Dismantling yields:

          Rolled Electromechanical Alloy Sheets x3

          Tinned Copper Wire & Windings x1

          Precision Drive Gear Blanks x1

          Heat-Resistant Ceramic Insulators x1

          Vulcanized Airtight Rubber Liners x4'
        UseCustomColor: 0
        CustomColor:
          R: 0.65
          G: 1
          B: 0.76
          A: 1
        WaitForContinue: 0
        DelayAfter: 0.15
      Choices:
      - Id: text_06_option_0
        Label: BACK TO ARCHIVE
        PlayerText: BACK TO ARCHIVE
        DisplayName: 
        UseCustomColor: 0
        CustomColor:
          R: 0.65
          G: 1
          B: 0.76
          A: 1
        NextNodeId: preview_home
        Conditions: []
        SetFlags: []
        Events: []
      NextNodeId: 
    - Id: text_07
      Title: Items/InsulationSleeve
      Lines:
      - Speaker: 2
        DisplayName: PREVIEW
        Text: 'Discarded Thermoelectric Insulation Sleeve


          Description:

          A thick, heavy cast-iron outer cylinder lined with large slabs of grayish-white insulating ceramic. Aged rubber gaskets are pressed into its seams, and dark brown marks from scorching heat stain the surface. It once encased a thermoelectric power core, insulating the surrounding hull structure from its fearsome heat. This outer sleeve is safe and provides heat-resistant material essential for building a power unit.


          Dismantling yields:

          Rolled Electromechanical Alloy Sheets x3

          Tinned Copper Wire & Windings x1

          Precision Drive Gear Blanks x1

          Heat-Resistant Ceramic Insulators x4

          Vulcanized Airtight Rubber Liners x2'
        UseCustomColor: 0
        CustomColor:
          R: 0.65
          G: 1
          B: 0.76
          A: 1
        WaitForContinue: 0
        DelayAfter: 0.15
      Choices:
      - Id: text_07_option_0
        Label: BACK TO ARCHIVE
        PlayerText: BACK TO ARCHIVE
        DisplayName: 
        UseCustomColor: 0
        CustomColor:
          R: 0.65
          G: 1
          B: 0.76
          A: 1
        NextNodeId: preview_home
